r":{"login":"BogdanZawr","id":37742044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQyMDQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37742044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanZawr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T18:06:27Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T18:06:27Z","body":"I also did fix for Jolt 3D ph engine, there is only 3 file changes (jolt_body_3d.cpp, jolt_body_3d.h, jolt_physics_direct_body_state_3d.cpp)\r\nbut i didnt include it here because im still working on it, and testing it.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4423446460/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4426187658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119353#issuecomment-4426187658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119353","id":4426187658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB9JDig","user":{"login":"BogdanZawr","id":37742044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQyMDQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37742044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanZawr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-12T00:13:14Z","updated_at":"2026-05-12T00:13:14Z","body":"Added a fix for Jolt Phisics too. there is the same issue in bouth","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4426187658/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4969753711","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119353#issuecomment-4969753711","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119353","id":4969753711,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKDhsbw","user":{"login":"voidexp","id":595098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NTA5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/595098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp","html_url":"https://github.com/voidexp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidexp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T13:34:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T04:02:45Z","body":"To me this solution is a very hacky and specific hotfix for platforms, it is bloated (the review has more AI generated comments than code), and doesn't address the real problem:\r\n\r\nWhen two bodies have a physics interaction dependent on one another, the one that is processed first (in creation order) accesses the \"outdated\" direct physics state from the previous tick of the other. Thus, if body A is processed before body B, but depends on the direct state of body B, it'll lag behind. \r\n\r\nThis is a problem in a lot of cases, for instance, if one wants to implement a master-puppet sort of scripted behavior in `integrate_forces()`.\r\n\r\nThe proper fix to me seems allowing to set the actual body processing order in the solver through the physics server API, and then one can implement any kind of dependency tracking via scripting by just changing that, instead of bringing that logic down to C++ level, introducing new virtual methods, and obscure caching of velocities and transforms.\r\n\r\nThe physics server knows nothing about the scene tree, and it shouldn't. \r\nThere's already the [PhysicsServer3D:body_set_collision_priority()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_physicsserver3d.html#class-physicsserver3d-method-body-set-collision-priority) method though, a similar low-level method could be introduced for allowing to set explicitly the solving order for bodies, that one can use then in scripting to match the `physics_process_priority` value.\r\n\r\nEDIT: This might be not really possible on solver level, for instance due to Jolt's multithreaded nature, perhaps the solution could be implemented in the server, to control when the direct state gets updated.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4969753711/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6029280036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119353#issuecomment-6029280036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119353","id":6029280036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZ1-DJA","user":{"login":"BogdanZawr","id":37742044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQyMDQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37742044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanZawr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanZawr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T02:00:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T02:00:00Z","body":"@voidexp \"When two bodies have a physics interaction dependent on one another, the one that is processed first (in creation order) accesses the \"outdated\" direct physics state from the previous tick of the other. Thus, if body A is processed before body B, but depends on the direct state of body B, it'll lag behind.\" - Valid comment. The code update I did creates the ordering flow in a scene_tree.cpp and automatically processes the one who is is_on_floor AFTER the one \"below. \" I know this is not the best fix, but this can help someone who is making a \"platformer\" and default CharacterBody3D lagging behind every time. I saw some good examples like this one [#101253 (comment) ](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101253#issuecomment-4422656070)\r\n\r\nI spent a lot of time testing and working on this issue, and I definitely will say that this is not an easy thing to fix . \" Creating a similar low-level method to set explicitly the solving order for bodies\" is a cool idea that I was thinking a lot about, but still, the solving order for bodies inside scene/main/scene_tree.cpp‎ needs to be done, and with a new low-level method , this can be done. However, the priority cannot be static , and calling it live inside every physics_process will add additional load. \r\n\r\n\r\nUpdate: Sadly, I can no longer support and update this ticket because I have moved to using a deterministic Rapier physics engine that solves all my needs right now. Therefore, I don't think I will be able to continue testing and updating this one. I hope someone who needs a fix for a simple platformer can take this idea and continue it, or I will inspire/help someone with the whole investigation I made.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6029280036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]